        // ── simd (register dependency): a scalar FP16 -> FP32 hardware
        // conversion inside an accumulating dot loop lowers (Clang 20.1.8
        // measured) to a lane-merge INTO the live accumulator — the loop
        // serializes on a false dependency — so the widening goes through
        // a once-built bit-pattern LUT whose reads land in fresh registers,
        // PER DIRECTION (the f32->f16 store keeps the intrinsic) ────────
        // Source: ggml/src/ggml-cpu/simd-mappings.h (the F16C block, the
